  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Description: \n\nWhen performing an animation and are locked in place, looking to the side and opening the main menu will result in your view snapping forward with your menu still to the side.\n\nReproduction:\n\nStep 1 - Open your radial menu and perform an animation (like a dance) that locks view and body to one spot while it is active\n\nStep 2 - While still in animation, look to your left or right as far as you can and open your main menu through the quick menu.\n\nStep 3 - This should make your view shoot forward while the menu stays where you were looking.\n\nNotes:\n\nI tested this on desktop.\n\nThe avatars I used to reproduce this were both 2.0 and 3.0 avatars.\n\nRestarting did not change the effect nor did any cache clearing.\n\nI cant tell if this has happened prior to the latest build or if this is new.",
